{
  "0": "Interest aggregation: in all four categories, replace the current readout r with 0.9r + 0.1m, where m is the normalized recency-weighted mean of valid GRU states, with weights 2^(-age/5). This small contribution may recover persistent interests without overwhelming recent intent. Preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, loss and training settings; mirror the readout in the predictor writer.",
  "1": "Feature construction: in all four categories, multiply each existing input embedding by 1.1 if that item appeared earlier in the supplied history prefix, otherwise by 1.0. Compute this indicator causally, excluding targets and padding. This deterministic repeat-interest feature may help the unchanged GRU distinguish recurring preferences from isolated interactions. Preserve embedding parameters and dimensions, topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; reproduce the feature at inference.",
  "2": "Learning objective: in all four categories, replace the current prediction loss with mean softplus(0.2 + negative_score - positive_score), using exactly the existing sampled negatives and valid training positions. A modest explicit margin may improve positive-versus-negative separation near the top-10 boundary without adding mining or scoring components. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU, readout, scoring, optimizer, sampling, scheduler and batch/epoch settings.",
  "3": "Training strategy: in all four categories, multiply the existing base learning rate by 0.7, preserving the current scheduler's relative multipliers and all other settings. Smaller updates may reduce the validation oscillation seen in Electronics while allowing the other categories to converge under unchanged early stopping and the 200-epoch cap. Keep optimizer type, batch size, dropout, weight decay, architecture, loss, seeds and evaluation fixed."
}
